# Gemini API key(s), called directly from the device (no backend to hold
# them server-side). EXPO_PUBLIC_ is required for Metro to inline these into
# the app bundle - see src/core/gemini/geminiClient.ts for where they're read,
# and the plan's note on why this means the key(s) are extractable from a
# built APK.
#
# KEY2 and KEY3 are optional. If set, every Gemini call (embeddings, hazard
# detection, vision find, severity scoring) round-robins across whichever of
# the three are present, spreading a free-tier per-key TPM/RPM quota across
# all of them - the same demo-day rate-limit mitigation api.py's
# /api/vision/find endpoint uses. Leave KEY2/KEY3 blank and everything just
# falls back to using KEY alone.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here
EXPO_PUBLIC_GEMINI_API_KEY2=
EXPO_PUBLIC_GEMINI_API_KEY3=
